<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH KOMERCNI '96 AFTER-TAX PROFIT RISES. [CORRECTED 16:13 GMT]</title>
<headline>CZECH KOMERCNI '96 AFTER-TAX PROFIT RISES. [CORRECTED 16:13 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary, unaudited results</p>
<p>for year ending December 31, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p>CALCULATED ACCORDING TO INTERNATIONAL ACCOUNTING STANDARDS</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit     5,372    vs     5,730</p>
<p>(Corrects pre-tax 1996 profit to 5,372 from 5,343)</p>
<p> After-tax profit   5,240    vs     5,111</p>
<p> Total Assets     448,254    vs   387,925</p>
<p> Basic Capital	9,502    vs     9,502</p>
<p>CALCULATED ACCORDING TO CZECH ACCOUNTING STANDARDS</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit     5,492    vs    5,781</p>
<p> After-tax profit   5,360    vs    5,162</p>
<p> Total Assets     460,881    vs  407,174</p>
<p> Basic Capital	9,502    vs    9,502</p>
<p>NOTE. Full company name is Komercni Banka a.s., the Czech</p>
<p>Republic's largest commercial bank.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
